WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.139
I'm Adrian, founder of ApplyArc,

2
00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:06.083
a UK job-search startup that
existed before this hackathon.

3
00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:09.693
Everything here was built
during it, on Meta's models.

4
00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.745
A real council job advert says: "Using AI?

5
00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:16.154
Please follow our guidance
to ensure your application

6
00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:18.984
reflects your own
knowledge and experience."

7
00:00:19.135 --> 00:00:20.257
Ana is fictional.

8
00:00:20.257 --> 00:00:21.576
Her problem is real.

9
00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:25.535
Three years in a Leeds care
home, working English every day,

10
00:00:25.535 --> 00:00:28.042
and a form that wants written English.

11
00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:30.797
She says it in Portuguese.

12
00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:34.181
Ana (synthetic voice, in
Portuguese): “Chamo-me Ana.

13
00:00:34.181 --> 00:00:36.897
Eu trabalho há três
anos num lar em Leeds…”

14
00:00:37.547 --> 00:00:40.447
Muse Voice Transcribe
writes it down, live,

15
00:00:40.447 --> 00:00:43.280
keeping her English care words in English.

16
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.101
She checks her words first.

17
00:00:45.252 --> 00:00:47.855
Muse Wonder turns her words into facts.

18
00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:50.324
Each one quotes her exact Portuguese.

19
00:00:50.324 --> 00:00:52.326
Code checks it, word for word.

20
00:00:52.326 --> 00:00:54.728
The English meaning sits underneath.

21
00:00:54.728 --> 00:00:55.929
She confirms both.

22
00:00:56.574 --> 00:01:01.219
Wonder checks the council's ten points
and finds the one she didn't cover:

23
00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:02.474
dignity and respect.

24
00:01:02.474 --> 00:01:03.855
It asks in Portuguese.

25
00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:06.065
Ana (synthetic voice, in
Portuguese): “Para mim,

26
00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.955
dignidade é bater à
porta antes de entrar…”

27
00:01:13.481 --> 00:01:18.053
Wonder drafts her supporting evidence
and a short letter, in English.

28
00:01:18.053 --> 00:01:21.367
Every factual sentence
cites a fact she confirmed,

29
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:25.210
and a second Wonder call checks
it against her Portuguese.

30
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:31.372
Then she remembers: only two of
her three years were nights.

31
00:01:31.372 --> 00:01:33.075
She says it once.

32
00:01:33.175 --> 00:01:34.766
Ana (synthetic voice,
in Portuguese):

33
00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:36.745
“Correção: os turnos da
noite foram dois anos,

34
00:01:36.745 --> 00:01:37.175
não três…”

35
00:01:41.679 --> 00:01:45.264
Wonder spots the contradiction
and asks which is right.

36
00:01:45.264 --> 00:01:46.893
She picks the correction.

37
00:01:46.893 --> 00:01:51.390
Only the sentences that cited the
old fact reopen, in both documents.

38
00:01:58.098 --> 00:02:03.189
Nothing gets submitted for her:
the pack is stamped NOT SUBMITTED.

39
00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:06.121
The employer gets one
page where every

40
00:02:06.121 --> 00:02:09.515
factual sentence opens
her Portuguese words.

41
00:02:09.665 --> 00:02:14.657
What Meta did, step by step: model,
host and Meta's request ids.

42
00:02:14.657 --> 00:02:16.686
Both models are weeks old.

43
00:02:16.686 --> 00:02:21.054
A verifier re-checks the record
without calling a model.

44
00:02:21.865 --> 00:02:27.887
The same loop runs on Meta's open
weights, Muse Spark Open, on Modal,

45
00:02:27.887 --> 00:02:31.466
so a care provider chooses where it runs.

46
00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.276
That's ApplyArc Evidence.

47
00:02:33.276 --> 00:02:33.873
Who pays?

48
00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:39.114
Councils and care employers who need
applications in the applicant's own words.

49
00:02:39.114 --> 00:02:42.033
It never screens, ranks
or submits anything.
